  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "lem:ovs-orthogonal-normal-signal",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(e=(u,c,c')\\in\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{OVS}}\\), every candidate nuisance \\(\\widetilde\\eta=(\\widetilde p,\\widetilde m)\\) with \\(\\widetilde p_{a,s}\\ge\\varepsilon/2\\) on all OVS-retained cells, and the signal in Definition \\(\\ref{def:orthogonal-ovs-normal-signal}\\),\n\\[\nE_P[S_e^{\\mathrm{OVS}}(O;\\widetilde\\eta)\\mid X]-g_e^{\\mathrm{OVS}}(X)\n=\\sum_{(a,s)\\in\\{(c,1),(c,0),(c',1),(c',0)\\}}\n\\sigma_{e,a,s}\\frac{\\widetilde p_{a,s}(X)-p_{a,s}(X)}{\\widetilde p_{a,s}(X)}\n\\{\\widetilde m_{a,s,u}(X)-m_{a,s,u}(X)\\},\n\\tag{35}\n\\]\nwhere \\((\\sigma_{e,c,1},\\sigma_{e,c,0},\\sigma_{e,c',1},\\sigma_{e,c',0})=(1,-1,-1,1)\\).  Hence the Gateaux derivative with respect to either nuisance at the truth is zero.  On the published OVS model, \\(g_e^{\\mathrm{OVS}}(X)=0\\) and \\(S_e^{\\mathrm{OVS}}(O;\\eta)=Z_{e,P}^{\\mathrm{OVS}}(O)\\) almost surely.  Since the number of rows is fixed,\n\\[\n\\|E_P[S^{\\mathrm{OVS}}(O;\\widetilde\\eta)\\mid X]-g^{\\mathrm{OVS}}(X)\\|_{P_X,2}\n\\le C_\\varepsilon\n\\|\\widetilde p-p\\|_{P_X,4}\\|\\widetilde m-m\\|_{P_X,4}.\n\\tag{36}\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "P",
      "X",
      "calEovs",
      "Sovs",
      "govs",
      "Zovs",
      "p",
      "m"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:orthogonal-ovs-normal-signal",
      "def:ovs-normal-projection",
      "thm:observable-equivalence",
      "ass:cell-overlap"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "For one signed cell term, conditional expectation gives\n\\[\nE_P\\left[\\widetilde m_{a,s,u}(X)\n+\\frac{\\mathbf 1_{a,s}}{\\widetilde p_{a,s}(X)}\n\\{\\Delta Y_u-\\widetilde m_{a,s,u}(X)\\}\\,\\middle|\\,X\\right]\n=\\widetilde m_{a,s,u}\n+\\frac{p_{a,s}}{\\widetilde p_{a,s}}(m_{a,s,u}-\\widetilde m_{a,s,u}).\n\\]\nSubtracting \\(m_{a,s,u}\\) turns the right side into\n\\[\n\\frac{\\widetilde p_{a,s}-p_{a,s}}{\\widetilde p_{a,s}}\n(\\widetilde m_{a,s,u}-m_{a,s,u}).\n\\]\nSumming with the four declared signs proves (35).  Every summand is a product of a propensity error and a regression error, so the derivative in either nuisance direction vanishes when the other nuisance is fixed at its truth.  The observable equivalence theorem gives \\(g_e^{\\mathrm{OVS}}=d_{c,u}-d_{c',u}=0\\), while substitution of \\(\\widetilde\\eta=\\eta\\) into the definition gives \\(S_e^{\\mathrm{OVS}}=Z_{e,P}^{\\mathrm{OVS}}\\).  Finally, clipping bounds every reciprocal by \\(2/\\varepsilon\\).  The triangle inequality followed by H\\\"older's inequality bounds each coordinate in \\(L_2(P_X)\\) by \\((2/\\varepsilon)\\|\\widetilde p-p\\|_4\\|\\widetilde m-m\\|_4\\).  Summing the fixed finite number of signed coordinates and rows proves (36).",
